Body:
I can't tell if the lack of noise in here is a good or bad thing haha

Not trying to start something but oooooof this sucks

@thdxr has his hands tied but we as the community can stand up

There's a workaround:

```ts
const myPlugin = async () => ({
  event: ({ event }) => {
    // the types are wrong here, "permission.asked" isn't listed there
    if (event.type === ("permission.asked" as "permission.updated")) {
      // do stuff
    }
  },
})
```

@nukeop @TestfireSoftware anthropic now requires different auth/request headers. This was likely done in sync with the legal request changes.

Plugin I just wrote, working for me without any further changes, just drop it into your plugin directory:
https://gist.github.com/gonzalosr/6ea39297fa73a62af1588306d0172d21
